PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
  • Data: web takes `vehicles: Vehicle[]`, fans `useQuery` out over `fetchVehicleState(id)`
    (`refetchInterval: 30_000`), and keeps the entries whose `state` resolved
    (`bars = filter(state !== null)`); native binds the same fleet + per-vehicle state +
    `useUnits` through the P1/S8 `BatteryComparisonSource` seam (production wraps the shared
    useVehicles + state + useUnits holders) — no HTTP in the view.
  • Tier: web `batteryColor(level)` (`>60 GOOD`, `>25 WARN`, else BAD) reproduced verbatim
    as `BatteryComparisonLevelStatus(level:)` + unit-asserted at the 60 / 25 boundaries
    (60 -> warning, 25 -> critical), mapped onto the P1/S9 status tokens.
  • Range: web `formatDistance(rated_range ?? 0)` is the SI converter (meters -> km/mi via
    `METERS_PER_KM=1000` / `METERS_PER_MILE=1609.344`, 1 fraction digit, locale grouping,
    `'—'` empty fallback); `BatteryComparisonRangeFormatter` ports it exactly + unit-asserts
    en_US goldens (268000 m -> "268.0 km", 1609.344 m -> "1.0 mi", 1_609_344 m -> "1,000.0 mi").
    SI on the wire; the conversion happens only at the render boundary (ADR-009 / Phase-42).
  • Name: web `display_name || vin` reproduced (empty display name falls back to VIN) +
    unit-asserted.
  • The web component renders NOTHING when no vehicle state resolves (`bars.length === 0 ->
    return null`). The Apple surface contract requires every state to render (never a blank
    box), so the dormant case becomes a calm "No vehicle battery data" panel and loading /
    error render inside the same always-present GlassPanel shell. The exact web null decision
    is preserved + unit-tested as `webRendersPanel(_:)` so the two never drift (documented
    enhancement, NOT silent drift).
  • Charts/maps: NONE in the web source — nothing to port to Swift Charts / MapKit.

